<Pack>
	<!--
		TWO TIERS, AND THE FILENAME SAYS WHICH.

		`Tutorial NN ` is the spine: ordered, numbered, each unit adding exactly one capability.
		Numbering is a CLAIM that order matters, so it is spent only here.

		`Prompt ` is the library: unordered, unnumbered, skippable, no prerequisites. Numbering
		these would make the numbers noise and make a reader arriving in the middle feel late -
		when the entire point of the tier is that they are not.

		The Coding Train states the same split in its own words: Main Tracks "you can follow like
		a course syllabus", Side Tracks "don't necessarily need to be watched in order".

		The prefixes extend vvvv's existing Explanation / HowTo / Example convention, which is
		already three-quarters of Diataxis. `Tutorial` is the genre those three are missing.
		tools\Test-VLPackage.ps1 checks the prefix, and checks this file against the disk in both
		directions.
	-->
	<Topic title="The course">
		<VLDocument link="Tutorial 01 Change how the world looks.vl" tags="map,mapsui,basemap,tile,xyz,url,template,style,appearance,attribution,licence,terrain,satellite,opentopomap,openstreetmap,cyclosm,sentinel,tutorial,spine,start,first" />
		<VLDocument link="Tutorial 04 Real data.vl" tags="geojson,map,mapsui,read,parse,feature,nts,netTopologySuite,style,styleByGeometry,label,marker,wgs84,mercator,projection,integration,packages,tutorial,spine" />
	</Topic>
